#document(
  default_font = "Helvetica",
  default_size = pt(11),
  page = { size = "letter", orientation = "portrait" },
  margin = { top = pt(72), right = pt(72), bottom = pt(72), left = pt(72) }
)

#style(
  name = "Normal",
  type = "paragraph",
  run = { font = "Helvetica", size = pt(11) },
  paragraph = { spacing = { before = pt(0), after = pt(8), line = { rule = "multiple", value = 1.15 } } }
)

#set paragraph(style = "Normal")

FOOTNOTE SPACING: footnotes stack at the foot of the page with the separator and paragraph spacing Word gives them.

The first claim needs a source#footnote[The first footnote is a single line.].

The second claim needs a longer note#footnote[The second footnote is long enough to wrap onto a second line at the foot of the page, which shows the line height inside a note.].

The third claim needs a short note#footnote[The third footnote.].
